            "body": "The reason seems to be that it is a code with nested same tags. It is the most visible condition at which Lua pattern based approach is not good. See [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/156#issuecomment-1308429031) for more information. And also [this other comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/110#issuecomment-1212277863) with a more proper tree-sitter based specification.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">The reason seems to be that it is a code with nested same tags. It is the most visible condition at which Lua pattern based approach is not good. See <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/156#issuecomment-1308429031\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/156/hovercard\">this comment</a> for more information. And also <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/110#issuecomment-1212277863\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/110/hovercard\">this other comment</a> with a more proper tree-sitter based specification.</p>",
